34,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"It turns out some of us have rooms that stay way colder than others, and people were even avoiding the cooler in summer to avoid arguments. We really need a system where we don't feel guilty for basic comfort.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The bills are incredibly volatile, with February being over three times the cost of August. Also, installing individual meters would be quite expensive, costing 34,000 yen per room plus annual maintenance.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Managing the money is a nightmare! At that other house, it took forty minutes just to log readings and split the total, and the reconciliation template was just a ton of manual data entry.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The monitor readings show a huge gap; the heaviest user draws four times more than the lightest. Also, the payment log shows several months were settled over two weeks late after people questioned the amounts.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"I also saw those late payments in the log. It seems like whenever the amount changes, it leads to queries and delays, which just creates tension between us.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, if the meters are that expensive, maybe we can find a way to be fair without spending a fortune upfront. We can't keep sitting in coats just to save money.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree that the upfront cost is a significant barrier. However, we must find a way to stabilize the monthly payments so they don't feel like a second rent during winter.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, if the difference in usage is that huge, maybe we need a system that doesn't require someone to spend their whole evening doing math just to be fair.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, that's the dilemma. If we just split it equally, the light users are subsidizing the heavy users, which is exactly what causes the tension and the late payments Misaki mentioned.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,Exactly. The tension comes from both the unfairness of the cost and the stress of the process. We need a solution that is simple enough to avoid arguments but fair enough to be accepted.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"If we just split everything equally, the people in the cold rooms will still feel like they're losing out. We need something that acknowledges the difference in our rooms without being a total headache.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"If we avoid the high cost of meters, we must find a way to handle the seasonal spikes. A system that smooths out the payments would prevent the winter shock I'm concerned about.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm really worried that if we pick something too complicated, the person in charge will just give up or get grumpy. We need a way to keep it running without it becoming a second job!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, if we don't account for the fact that some of us use four times more power, we're just replacing one kind of tension with another. We can't ignore the actual usage data.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"But if we focus only on the usage data, we might end up in a cycle of constant questioning and late payments. We need a method that feels final and transparent.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,I think we're all seeing the same problem from different angles. We need a way to handle the seasonal spikes and the usage gaps without making the monthly process a total nightmare for whoever manages it.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Precisely. We need a solution that balances financial predictability, fairness in usage, and administrative simplicity. It seems we are all in agreement that the current system is unsustainable.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I just hope whatever we choose doesn't involve a giant spreadsheet that takes hours to fill out! Let's make sure the ""simplicity"" part is actually real.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I agree. If we can't find a way to make the data entry effortless, we'll just be back to arguing over the totals every single month.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,Let's hope the options we're about to see provide a way to move past these arguments and restore some peace to the house.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
