59,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"So we have three options: a Seasonal Fixed Rate, Per-Room Metering, or a Flat Household Share. Given how cold some rooms get, I'm leaning toward something that doesn't make us feel guilty for using heat.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The Seasonal Fixed Rate seems most appealing to me. It would eliminate the winter spikes and provide the financial predictability I need, without the exorbitant upfront cost of meters.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I'm worried about the Per-Room Metering. Based on what I saw at the other house, that sounds like a total nightmare to manage every month. I'd much rather have something simpler.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"A Flat Household Share is too simplistic; it ignores the usage gaps I found. Per-Room Metering is the only way to be truly fair, provided we can handle the administration.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"I'm concerned that a Flat Household Share will just keep the same tensions alive. However, Per-Room Metering sounds like it could lead to more accusations. I think the Seasonal Fixed Rate might be the most peaceful.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I understand wanting it to be fair, but if we use meters, will we just go back to arguing over every single yen? I think the Seasonal Fixed Rate sounds much more relaxed.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the cost of installing those meters is simply too high to justify. A Seasonal Fixed Rate achieves stability without requiring a massive initial investment from everyone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, please think about the time it takes! If we have to log readings every month, it's going to be a chore that someone hates. The Seasonal Fixed Rate sounds way easier.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, I hear you, but ""easier"" isn't the same as ""fair."" If we go with a fixed rate, the heavy users still win and the light users still lose. We need a real solution.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"But if ""real solutions"" lead to the late payments and resentment I saw in the logs, are they actually solutions? The Seasonal Fixed Rate removes the monthly shock and the constant questioning.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I agree with Misaki. If we're all happy and not stressing over the bill, that's more important than perfect precision. I'm voting for the Seasonal Fixed Rate.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I also vote for the Seasonal Fixed Rate. It is the only option that addresses the volatility of the bills while remaining financially viable for all of us.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for the Seasonal Fixed Rate too! It sounds like the only way to keep the peace and save us from a mountain of paperwork.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I cannot in good conscience vote for a system that ignores the usage gap. However, since the majority is against it, I'll vote for Per-Room Metering to stand by the principle of fairness.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'll vote for the Seasonal Fixed Rate. It seems like the best way to stop the cycle of accusations and late payments while keeping things simple for everyone.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,It looks like we've reached a consensus! I'm glad we could find a way to make the house feel more comfortable for everyone without making it a chore.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. The Seasonal Fixed Rate provides the stability and predictability we need. I am satisfied that we have reached a rational decision that balances our various concerns.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,Yay! No more scary spreadsheets or spending my whole evening doing math. I'm just happy we're all on the same page now!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I still think we're ignoring the core issue of usage, but I can't fight the majority. As long as we're honest during the year-end settlement, I'll accept it.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I'm just glad we've found a way to prioritize our relationships over the numbers. Let's hope this brings some peace back to our home.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
